>> source: https://bellyfull.net/bread-and-butter-pickles/#wprm-recipe-container-35237
>> serves: 16
>> prep time: 15 minutes
>> cook time: 5 minutes
>> total time: 1520 minutes

Combine @pickling cucumbers sliced 1/4-inch thick (which is about 5.5 cups){1.5%lbs} and @coarse salt{1.5%Tbsp} in a large, shallow #bowl{}; cover and chill ~{1.5%hours}.

Move cucumbers into a #colander{} and rinse thoroughly under cold water. Drain well, and return cucumbers to #bowl{}.

Add @thinly sliced sweet onion{1%cup} to the #bowl{} and toss with the cucumbers.

Combine the @granulated sugar{1%cup}, @white vinegar{1%cup}, @apple cider vinegar{0.5%cup}, @light brown sugar{0.25%cup}, @mustard seeds{1.5%tsp}, @celery seeds{0.5%tsp} and @ground turmeric{1/8%tsp} in a #medium saucepan{}; bring to a simmer over medium heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves.

Pour the hot vinegar mixture over cucumber mixture; let stand at room temperature ~{1%hour}.

Cover and refrigerate ~{24%hours}. (If you’re really impatient, though, they taste great after only a few hours!)

Store in an #airtight container{} in refrigerator up to 1 month.
